["document.info", {"title": "Nest box from one plank", "author": "3DCraft Jigs", "licence": "CC-BY-4.0", "description": "A nest box for a garden bird of the Low Countries, sawn from one plank and screwed together. Pick the species: the entrance, the floor, the height and the shape come from Vogelbescherming Nederland's table of nest boxes. Set your plank; the Jig refuses a plank too narrow or too short for that bird. For sawing, select the sketch Plank plan in Features and export the selection as DXF or SVG: the plank with every board along it in sawing order, labelled. For marking out, File > Export, Sheet of set: Board layout (DXF or SVG): every board and guard plate at true size. The Outputs give the plank length needed and how many boards to saw.", "tags": ["woodwork", "garden", "birds", "nest box", "cut list"]}],
